---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { hecklers, stats } from '../data/site';
import officeImg from '../assets/office-chaos.webp';
import profileImg from '../assets/steve-profile.webp';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Steve Martin, The Other One | Gobiya SEO Los Angeles"
  description="Steve Martin (the SEO one) has been building websites since 1996, running SEO since Google's early years, and answering for his name for longer than that. BBB A+ rated. No account managers. Based in Los Angeles."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="hero-eyebrow eyebrow">The Bio · Act One</p>
          <h1>The other<br /><span class="accent">Steve Martin.</span></h1>
          <p class="hero-sub">
            Building websites since 1996, and one lifetime of explaining that no,
            <em>I cannot get you tickets</em>.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-creds">
            <span class="cred-pill">BBB A+</span>
            <span class="cred-pill">Est. 2010</span>
            <span class="cred-pill">Los Angeles</span>
            <span class="cred-pill">Bilingual EN / ES</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <figure class="stage-frame">
          <Image
            src={officeImg}
            alt="Steve Martin in a suit holding floppy disks and a vintage microphone, papers flying, whiteboards covered in growth charts behind him"
            widths={[480, 800, 1200]}
            sizes="(max-width: 940px) 92vw, 520px"
            loading="eager"
          />
          <figcaption>
            My actual tech stack. The floppy disks are for the clients who ask if I back things up.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="bulb-strip" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <!-- Stats bar -->
  <section class="playbill" style="padding-bottom: 0;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="stats reveal">
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="num">1996</div>
          <div class="label">First website. Visitor counter. Background tile. Peak UX.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="num">25+ yrs</div>
          <div class="label">Web dev & SEO experience — since before "SEO" was a word</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="num">1.4M</div>
          <div class="label">URI paths analyzed in a single forensic scan</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="num">92%</div>
          <div class="label">Algorithm recovery rate. Median time: six weeks.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Main bio -->
  <section class="playbill">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head" style="max-width:none;">
        <p class="eyebrow">The Long Version</p>
        <h2>How this happened.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="prose reveal">
        <p>
          I built my first website in 1996 at AT&T WorldNet in Burbank, helping businesses put
          themselves on the internet for the first time. The sites had visitor counters, tiled
          backgrounds, and lines of text that said "best viewed in Netscape Navigator." They were,
          at the time, genuinely impressive.
        </p>

        <p>
          From 2000 to 2005 I was at Webcastr.com in West Hollywood, building a video content
          distribution platform for Sony Music artists — engineering and organic search practiced
          side by side from the start, before anyone had a word for what we were doing.
        </p>

        <p>
          Then came the in-house years: internet marketing and website management for a plumbing
          company in Los Angeles, where I learned that a top Google Maps ranking for "emergency
          plumber" at 2 AM is worth more than any award in a lobby display case. In 2010 I founded
          Gobiya to do that work professionally, and incorporated it as Gobiya LLC in 2012.
        </p>

        <p>
          I have also had this name the entire time. For the first thirty years it was a punchline
          at the DMV. Then I started doing this for a living and discovered that a memorable name
          is, professionally speaking, an unfair advantage. Nobody forgets who did their website.
        </p>

        <h3>What the work actually looks like</h3>

        <p>
          Gobiya is not a roster of account managers. It is an engineering practice with one name
          on the work. You talk to me. Not a salesperson who disappears after the contract, not an
          account manager who forwards your email to a contractor eleven time zones away. I do the
          audit, I write the plan, I do the work, and when something does not go the way I said it
          would, I am the one who tells you.
        </p>

        <p>
          I take a small number of clients on purpose. It is the only way the above stays true.
          When I am full, I will tell you I am full and point you to somebody good — a sentence
          most agencies are physically incapable of saying.
        </p>

        <h3>Documented results</h3>

        <p>
          Five times the patient inquiries for a dental practice. Forty-five percent organic
          traffic growth for a home remodeling company. 5.7× Google Ads ROAS for a windows and
          doors company. A sixty-one percent reduction in cost per lead for a B2B SaaS company.
          These are not projections on a slide deck. They are what happened.
        </p>

        <h3>The name thing</h3>

        <p>
          Yes, I know. No, I have never played the banjo. Yes, someone has sung
          <em>King Tut</em> at me on a discovery call. He is a client now, so I suppose it
          worked.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Career timeline -->
  <section class="playbill" style="padding-top: 0;">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">The Record · Act Two</p>
        <h2>25 years of search, engineering, and staying ahead of the curve.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline reveal">

        <div class="tl-item">
          <div class="tl-meta">
            <span class="tl-year">1996–2000</span>
            <span class="tl-act">The Start</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-body">
            <h3 class="tl-title">Web tech at AT&T WorldNet</h3>
            <p class="tl-desc">
              Helped businesses build their first websites in Burbank before most people had
              heard of a homepage. Earned a Certificate in Website Design from Glendale Career
              College in 1996. Visitor counters included at no extra charge.
            </p>
            <div class="tl-tags">
              <span class="tl-tag">AT&T WorldNet</span>
              <span class="tl-tag">Glendale Career College</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tl-item">
          <div class="tl-meta">
            <span class="tl-year">2000–2005</span>
            <span class="tl-act">The Platform</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-body">
            <h3 class="tl-title">Sony Music & Webcastr.com</h3>
            <p class="tl-desc">
              Built a video content distribution platform for Sony Music artists at Webcastr.com
              in West Hollywood — engineering and organic search practiced side by side from the
              start, before anyone had a job title for it.
            </p>
            <div class="tl-tags">
              <span class="tl-tag">Sony Music</span>
              <span class="tl-tag">Web Development</span>
              <span class="tl-tag">Organic Search</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tl-item">
          <div class="tl-meta">
            <span class="tl-year">2005–2010</span>
            <span class="tl-act">The Field</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-body">
            <h3 class="tl-title">In-house SEO & digital marketing</h3>
            <p class="tl-desc">
              Led internet marketing and website management for Mr. Speedy Plumbing &amp; Rooter
              in Los Angeles, achieving top Google Maps rankings for primary plumbing terms across
              the city. Learned that rank at 2 AM is worth more than any agency retainer.
            </p>
            <div class="tl-tags">
              <span class="tl-tag">Local SEO</span>
              <span class="tl-tag">Google Maps</span>
              <span class="tl-tag">Lead Generation</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tl-item">
          <div class="tl-meta">
            <span class="tl-year">2010</span>
            <span class="tl-act">The Agency</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-body">
            <h3 class="tl-title">Gobiya is founded in Los Angeles</h3>
            <p class="tl-desc">
              Founded to specialize in the intersection of technical web development and organic
              search — recovering sites from algorithm updates, building custom React sites, and
              managing paid media for businesses that need measurable results. Incorporated as
              Gobiya LLC in 2012. BBB A+ rated.
            </p>
            <div class="tl-tags">
              <span class="tl-tag">Technical SEO</span>
              <span class="tl-tag">React Development</span>
              <span class="tl-tag">Performance Marketing</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tl-item">
          <div class="tl-meta">
            <span class="tl-year">2011–2023</span>
            <span class="tl-act">The Updates</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-body">
            <h3 class="tl-title">Every algorithm cycle, inside live accounts</h3>
            <p class="tl-desc">
              Panda, Penguin, Hummingbird, Medic, BERT, the Helpful Content Update, and the 2024
              core updates — each tracked inside active client accounts, not read about afterward
              in a blog post. Documented recovery rate: 92%. Median time from diagnosis to
              restored rankings: six weeks. URI paths analyzed in a single scan: 1.4 million.
            </p>
            <div class="tl-tags">
              <span class="tl-tag">Recovery Forensics</span>
              <span class="tl-tag">92% Recovery Rate</span>
              <span class="tl-tag">1.4M URI Scans</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tl-item tl-item--current">
          <div class="tl-meta">
            <span class="tl-year">2024 → now</span>
            <span class="tl-act">The AI Era</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tl-body">
            <h3 class="tl-title">Search becomes answers</h3>
            <p class="tl-desc">
              Google AI Overviews arrived in 2024 and began intercepting clicks from sites that
              rank well but are invisible in AI-generated answers. Gobiya added GEO (Generative
              Engine Optimization) — content and entity structure built to be cited by ChatGPT,
              Perplexity, and Google AI Overviews. Your competitors are still updating their
              meta descriptions.
            </p>
            <div class="tl-tags">
              <span class="tl-tag">GEO / AI Citations</span>
              <span class="tl-tag">Google AI Overviews</span>
              <span class="tl-tag">Structured Data</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Credentials card -->
  <section class="about">
    <div class="wrap">
      <Image
        src={profileImg}
        alt="Steve Martin, SEO consultant and founder of Gobiya, Los Angeles"
        widths={[240, 480]}
        sizes="240px"
        class="headshot"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--text-inverse-muted);">The Short Version</p>
        <h2>One person. One name on the work. No delegation.</h2>
        <div class="cred-grid">
          <div class="cred-row">
            <span class="cred-key">Founded</span>
            <span class="cred-val">Est. 2010 · Gobiya LLC 2012 · Los Angeles, CA</span>
          </div>
          <div class="cred-row">
            <span class="cred-key">Background</span>
            <span class="cred-val">AT&T WorldNet (1996) · Sony Music / Webcastr.com (2000–2005) · SEO since 2005</span>
          </div>
          <div class="cred-row">
            <span class="cred-key">Specialty</span>
            <span class="cred-val">Algorithm recovery · Technical SEO · Local SEO · Google Ads · React dev · GEO for AI</span>
          </div>
          <div class="cred-row">
            <span class="cred-key">Dev stack</span>
            <span class="cred-val">React · Next.js · Vite · Tailwind · Supabase · WordPress</span>
          </div>
          <div class="cred-row">
            <span class="cred-key">Languages</span>
            <span class="cred-val">English · Spanish (bilingual)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="cred-row">
            <span class="cred-key">Credentials</span>
            <span class="cred-val">Google-certified (2015–2019) · <a href="https://www.bbb.org/us/ca/los-angeles/profile/digital-marketing/gobiya-llc-1216-495569" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BBB A+ rated</a> · Gobiya LLC</span>
          </div>
          <div class="cred-row">
            <span class="cred-key">Paid media</span>
            <span class="cred-val">Google Ads · Bing Ads · Meta Ads · Yelp Ads — up to $15K/month managed</span>
          </div>
          <div class="cred-row">
            <span class="cred-key">LinkedIn</span>
            <span class="cred-val"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/stevemartingobiya/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">linkedin.com/in/stevemartingobiya</a></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="credit-line">
          Building websites since 1996 · Zero SNL appearances · One search result at a time
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Hecklers FAQ -->
  <section class="playbill">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Hecklers Welcome</p>
        <h2>Questions I get shouted at me.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="heckle-list reveal">
        {
          hecklers.map((item) => (
            <details class="heckle">
              <summary>{item.q}</summary>
              <p class="answer">{item.a}</p>
            </details>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">One Night Only</span>
      <h2>Enough about me.</h2>
      <p>Tell me what your website is doing to you and I will tell you how to stop it.</p>
      <a href="/contact" class="ticket-btn">Book Your Free Consult →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Hero credential pills */
  .hero-creds {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 20px;
  }
  .cred-pill {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    box-shadow: 2px 2px 0 var(--border);
    padding: 5px 10px;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--bg);
  }

  /* Timeline */
  .timeline {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--border);
    margin-left: 8px;
  }
  .tl-item {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 130px 1fr;
    gap: 24px;
    padding: 0 0 36px 28px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .tl-item::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: -7px;
    top: 4px;
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
  }
  .tl-item--current::before {
    background: var(--surface-dark);
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .timeline { margin-left: 0; border-left: none; }
    .tl-item {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 8px;
      padding-left: 0;
      border-left: 3px solid var(--border);
      padding-left: 18px;
      margin-bottom: 4px;
    }
    .tl-item::before { display: none; }
  }
  .tl-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
    padding-top: 2px;
  }
  .tl-year {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .tl-act {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .tl-title {
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }
  .tl-desc {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  .tl-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  .tl-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 9.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding: 3px 8px;
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
  }

  /* Credentials grid in the dark about section */
  .cred-grid {
    margin-top: 18px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
    border: 2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.15);
  }
  .cred-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 110px 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .cred-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .cred-key {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-inverse-muted);
    padding-top: 2px;
  }
  .cred-val {
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.88);
  }
  .cred-val a {
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.88);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .cred-val a:hover { color: #fff; }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .cred-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2px;
    }
  }
</style>
